3. **Date-stamped review note:** Include "Last reviewed: July 2026" in the article header or footer. Identify HUD enforcement statistics as the most time-sensitive claims in this article.

### 6b. Expertise Signals

- State that HUD disability-related complaints consistently represent the single largest category of fair housing complaints filed each year (cite "as of fiscal year 2024 HUD data").
- Specify the exact date threshold for design-and-construction requirements: March 13, 1991.
- Include the specific statute reference: 42 U.S.C. § 3604(f)(3)(C) for design requirements, and 42 U.S.C. § 3604 for prohibited conduct.
- Distinguish between the one-year HUD filing window and the two-year private lawsuit window. This specific distinction appears in AI responses but is missing from several competitor pages.
- Clarify that design-and-construction violations are treated as ongoing by courts (no standard statute of limitations applies to the structural non-compliance itself). This is expert-level detail not covered by most competitors.

